# Audited 2026-09-11, clean-up C2e. Every rule below is annotated with what it hides. Most match
# nothing in a clean tree, which is the point; a rule that can never match is the defect to look
# for. This file has been silently inert before: every line carried a trailing comma from the start
# of the project, so no rule matched anything, and a duplicate mutants/ tree, coverage databases and
# build artifacts were tracked for months. Do not add a rule here without saying what it hides.
#
# Comments must be on their own line. A `#` after a pattern is part of the pattern, not a comment,
# which is how the last rule below is written on purpose.
#
# One rule interacts with the Stop hook. .claude/hooks/stop-check.sh hashes the gated tree with
# `git ls-files -c -o --exclude-standard`, so anything ignored here is invisible to that hash even
# when it sits inside a gated path. mutants/ is such a path: it is in GATED_PATHS and ignored, so it
# contributes nothing to the hash and never will. That is right as things stand — the directory is
# mutmut's scratch sandbox, generated per run and never committed — but the two lists disagree on
# paper, and if mutants/ ever holds anything a gate reads, one of them has to change.

# local virtualenv; the toolchain itself is declared in requirements-dev.txt
.venv/
# harness state: events.jsonl, last-green-tree, coverage.json, mutation-backup/. Not committed, so
# a verdict survives only on disk; docs/queue-history/events-prototype-1.jsonl is the tag's copy.
.gauntlet/
# mutmut's scratch sandbox, regenerated per run; see the note above about the gated-tree hash
mutants/
# mutmut's warm cache; a stale one understates a score
.mutmut-cache
# bytecode
__pycache__/
# pytest state
.pytest_cache/
# coverage's own database; the coverage gate reads .gauntlet/coverage.json instead
.coverage
# SQLite files from a local run of the shell
*.db
# build metadata; the package is never installed here, conftest.py puts src/ on sys.path
*.egg-info/
# an editor's backup of the pinned toolchain
requirements-dev.txt.bak
# LibreOffice lock files, from opening an exported review sheet
.~lock.*#
